    "result_text": "The build passes and all tests are green. The full test suite consists of the 3 `AcceptanceTest` cases (the other files are an abstract base and a helper), all passing.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the optional, validated-when-present `postcode` field for owners:\n\n**API contract** (`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`)\n- Added a `postcode` property to the `OwnerFields` schema \u2014 a 4-digit string (`^[0-9]{4}$`), not in the `required` list, so it stays backward-compatible. Because `Owner` is `allOf [OwnerFields, \u2026]`, this makes `postcode` both an accepted input and a returned field in the generated DTOs.\n\n**Domain + persistence**\n- `Owner.java`: added the `postcode` column, field, getter, and setter.\n- Added a `postcode` column to all four schema dialects (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`). Tests run on hsqldb.\n- MapStruct maps `postcode` automatically in both directions (name match; it isn't in any `@Mapping(ignore)` list).\n\n**Validation \u2192 400** (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`)\n- Added a fixed city\u2192region table (Sydney=NSW, Melbourne=VIC, Brisbane=QLD) and region\u2192range table (NSW 2000-2099, VIC 3000-3099, QLD 4000-4099).\n- `validatePostcode(city, postcode)` is called during `addOwner`: a null/blank postcode is skipped (optional when absent); a present postcode must be 4 digits, and when the city has a known region it must fall in that region's inclusive range. A city with no known region accepts any 4-digit postcode. Violations throw the new `InvalidPostcodeException`.\n- Added `InvalidPostcodeException` and its `@ExceptionHandler` in `ExceptionControllerAdvice`, returning 400 with `postcode` in the `errors` array (mirroring the existing telephone/email handlers). The generated `@Pattern` also rejects malformed values like `\"12\"` with 400 as a first line of defense.\n\nTest results: `Tests run: 3, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `coreStoresValidPostcode`, `coreAcceptsOwnerWithoutPostcode`, and `errorRejectsMalformedPostcode` all pass.",
